{"body":"## Finding\n\nOf **1,864** records graded `EXACT_MATCH`, **356** carry a CHEBI term whose\nprimary label equals neither the record's `preferred_term` nor any recorded\nsynonym. Resolving each against the local `chebi.db` synonym lists splits them\ncleanly:\n\n| | count | |\n|---|---|---|\n| justified by a ChEBI **synonym** | **297** | term is right, **grade is wrong** |\n| matched by **nothing** in ChEBI (label or synonym) | **59** | needs individual review |\n\n## The 297 are mis-graded by the schema's own definition\n\n`mediaingredientmech.yaml` is unambiguous:\n\n```yaml\nEXACT_MATCH:    Direct exact match to ontology term\nSYNONYM_MATCH:  Matches known synonym in ontology\n```\n\nA label matching a ChEBI *synonym* rather than the primary label is\n`SYNONYM_MATCH` by definition. This is not a judgement call — it is 16% of all\n`EXACT_MATCH` records disagreeing with the enum they use.\n\nThe grade is load-bearing: it is what tells a downstream consumer how much to\ntrust an identity assertion, and `EXACT_MATCH` is the strongest claim available.\n\n## The 59 need review, and are not one thing\n\nSub-classes visible on inspection:\n\n- **Genuine scope loss** — the label carries a qualifier the term does not:\n  `b-Glucan from Oat` → `beta-D-glucan` (source lost),\n  `amylopectin from maize` → `amylopectin`,\n  `Acetate (carbon source)` → `acetate`,\n  `Ammonium chloride (nitrogen source)` → `ammonium chloride`,\n  `Alpha-Toxicarol (Dl)` → `Toxicarol` (racemate → unspecified).\n- **A semantic error** — `Aromatic hydrocarbon` → `polycyclic arene`. Not a\n  synonym relation in either direction: benzene is an aromatic hydrocarbon and\n  is not polycyclic. The term is narrower than the label.\n- **Trivial-vs-systematic naming**, arguably fine but not *exact*:\n  `Butanol` → `butan-1-ol`, `2-Ethylhexanol` → `2-ethylhexan-1-ol`,\n  `2-Piperidinone` → `piperidin-2-one`.\n- **Formula-as-label**: `KNO2` → `potassium nitrite`, `NH42CO3` →\n  `ammonium carbonate`. The formula is not a ChEBI string at all.\n- **Misspellings that nonetheless resolved correctly**:\n  `Pyromelitic acid` → `pyromellitic acid`, `Thioglycollic acid` →\n  `thioglycolic acid`. Compound is right; `EXACT_MATCH` is not.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```python\n# for each EXACT_MATCH record with a CHEBI ontology_id:\n#   skip if preferred_term or a recorded synonym == ontology_label (normalised)\n#   else look up the term's synonyms in ~/.data/oaklib/chebi.db:\n#     any match -> should be SYNONYM_MATCH   (297)\n#     no match  -> review                     (59)\n```\n\nNormalisation is case- and punctuation-insensitive, so this does not flag mere\ncapitalisation differences.\n\n## Suggested action\n\nThe 297 are a safe mechanical re-grade to `SYNONYM_MATCH` with a\n`curation_history` entry — no ontology_id changes, no SSSOM object changes.\nNote the SSSOM predicate may need review alongside it, since `skos:exactMatch`\nrows resting on a synonym match are the same overstatement.\n\nThe 59 need per-record calls; the scope-loss and `Aromatic hydrocarbon` cases\nare real defects, the naming-convention ones probably just want re-grading too.\n\n## Provenance\n\nSurfaced by the Claude research lane, which flagged `EXACT_MATCH` as\nunsupportable on `1-naphtylacetic_Acid`, `5-Hydroxyoctanoate`, `Angustmycin` and\n`Aluminium_Sulfate` independently, then generalised repo-wide against chebi.db.\nRelated: #309, #312, #315, #316.","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABQOWR-Q","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"**Re-measured 2026-08-22 against `main`. The numbers here are stale rather than wrong — most of this shipped.**\n\n`scripts/regrade_synonym_matches.py` landed with **157 re-grades applied** in #325. Reproducing this issue's own stated method from scratch now finds ~142 more candidates, which reconciles with the original 297 (297 − 157 ≈ 140). But the committed script — which additionally skips records whose only evidence is *circular* — reports **25** remaining:\n\n```\nnot_exact_match          903\nnot_chebi                163\nlabel_matches           1335\nno_chebi_synonym_match    49\ncircular_evidence_only    90\ndeeper_defect_skipped      1\nregrade                   25\n```\n\nSo the re-grade half is **25 records from done**, not 297.\n\n## The residual is 235, not 59 — and it is five different problems\n\nThe \"matches nothing in ChEBI\" set is far larger than this issue estimated. Categorised:\n\n| n | disposition | example |\n|---:|---|---|\n| 90 | trivial-vs-systematic naming | `2-Piperidinone` → `piperidin-2-one` |\n| 61 | **formula-as-label** | `Alcl3_X_6_H2o` → `aluminium trichloride hexahydrate` |\n| 40 | scope loss (record has a qualifier the term lacks) | `Acetate_Carbon_Source` → `acetate` |\n| 38 | qualified name (salt / solution / from-X) | `05_M_Nitrilotriacetic_Acid_Disodium_Salt` → `sodium nitrilotriacetate` |\n| 6 | term more specific than the record | `Alanosine` → `L-alanosine`; `D` → `sodium lactate` (plainly wrong) |\n\nTwo things follow:\n\n- The **61 formula-as-label** are the `capitalize()` scars (#147 / #443) and overlap the hydrate family (#321, #334). They can never match a ChEBI string because the \"name\" is a formula, so no synonym-based rule will ever clear them — they want doing **with** the hydrate work, not here.\n- The target grade differs per class, so this is not one mechanical pass. `SYNONYM_MATCH` is wrong for all five (no synonym exists); the naming classes want `LEXICAL_MATCH`, the scope-loss ones want `NARROW_MATCH` or `CLOSE_MATCH`.\n\n## One more correction\n\nOf the synonym-justified matches, **every one rests on `oio:hasRelatedSynonym`; none on `hasExactSynonym`**. Spot-checked and they do look like genuine identity (`2-mercaptoethanesulfonate` → `CHEBI:17905` coenzyme M; `2-chloro-4-ethylamino-6-isopropylamino-1,3,5-triazine` → `CHEBI:15930` atrazine), but it is a weaker justification than this issue implies and worth stating.\n\nNote for anyone reproducing: semsql stores subjects as **CURIEs**, not IRIs. Querying `statements` by IRI returns nothing, which reads exactly like \"this term has no synonyms\" — it silently produced a 0/377 split before I caught it.","createdAt":"2026-08-23T02:15:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/317#issuecomment-5383754233","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABQPdZRw","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"The recipe grouping/hierarchy audit found a preventive source for this issue that\nis not covered by #438.\n\n`scripts/import_from_culturemech.py:96-104` translates CultureMech\n`DIRECT_MATCH` directly to MIM `EXACT_MATCH`. CultureMech's current aggregate\nproducer assigns `mapping_quality: DIRECT_MATCH` as a default assumption\n(`CultureMech/scripts/aggregate_mapped_ingredients.py:242-249`), after grouping\noccurrences by preferred term. The import boundary therefore cannot tell whether\nthe underlying ontology hit used a primary label, a synonym, or a weaker lexical\npath. That is a plausible regeneration path for synonym-supported records being\ngraded `EXACT_MATCH` again after the current correction.\n\nImportant correction to the original suggested SSSOM follow-up: #438's Rule D\nand this issue cover independent axes.\n\n- `mapping_quality` says how the ontology grounding was established.\n- The identity-row predicate says that a MIM subject is identical to its own\n  primary `identifier`.\n\nA correctly regraded `SYNONYM_MATCH` record must still publish\n`skos:exactMatch` on the row whose object is its own identifier. Consequently,\n#438 cannot surface #317, and changing synonym-supported identity rows to\n`skos:closeMatch` would reintroduce the defect #438 fixed.\n\nSuggested prevention criteria to add here:\n\n- preserve the source match method end to end, or recompute primary-label versus\n  ontology-synonym evidence at import;\n- import a primary-label hit as `EXACT_MATCH` and an ontology-synonym hit as\n  `SYNONYM_MATCH`;\n- report ambiguous/unmatched strings instead of defaulting them to exact;\n- test that regrading mapping quality never changes the own-identifier identity\n  predicate.\n\n","createdAt":"2026-08-23T07:50:27Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/317#issuecomment-5384919367","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":317,"state":"CLOSED","title":"297 records graded EXACT_MATCH are synonym matches; 59 more match nothing in ChEBI","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/317"}
